WEBVTT

00:12.451 --> 00:14.581
1970

00:14.581 --> 00:17.837
UNION ISOLATION FACILITY,
ROOM 1859

02:21.962 --> 02:23.716
2020

02:23.716 --> 02:25.469
AUGUST 4TH

02:25.469 --> 02:27.223
LATE NIGHT

02:50.227 --> 02:53.651
Whaddaya think?
This yacht handles like a dream, right?

02:55.905 --> 03:00.832
This baby’s souped up,
so we’ll reach Vladivostok in no ti-

03:01.332 --> 03:02.752
What the heck are you doing?

03:03.044 --> 03:05.592
Didn’t you hear what that guy said?

03:05.758 --> 03:09.516
Of course, there will be people
hunting you along the way.

03:09.516 --> 03:12.187
Here’s hoping you both make
it over there in one piece.

03:12.731 --> 03:15.319
About how they’ll be hunting us
the entire way there...

03:16.822 --> 03:18.116
So what?

03:18.450 --> 03:21.372
This is my boat!
Come out and enjoy the ride!

03:21.372 --> 03:23.544
No! I’m scared!

03:23.544 --> 03:26.382
We could be attacked at any moment!

03:26.592 --> 03:30.600
Quit bein’ a buzzkill. Even if that does happen,
a little partying on deck ain’t gonna kill y-

03:30.600 --> 03:31.267
Huh?

03:32.687 --> 03:33.939
See, I told you!

03:33.939 --> 03:36.319
Tch! Couldn’t even get one drink in, huh?

03:38.574 --> 03:39.910
But man, they’re such lousy shots!

03:44.961 --> 03:46.924
If they keep this up,
it’ll be smooth sailing to Russia!

03:47.174 --> 03:50.932
Are you kidding me?
This boat’s sure to get blasted to pieces!

03:50.932 --> 03:53.604
If that happens,
we can blow outta here with your unluck!

03:53.604 --> 03:56.777
My unluck doesn’t conveniently work like that!

03:56.777 --> 03:58.238
It’s all about how you use it!

04:00.033 --> 04:03.164
My Undead ability isn’t just about death prevention!

04:05.293 --> 04:08.676
If I cut a part of my body nearly off
and make it grow back in place...

04:08.968 --> 04:10.178
...it becomes a weapon!

04:11.765 --> 04:13.435
Parts Bullet Fist!

04:18.529 --> 04:19.990
Y-You did it!

04:20.240 --> 04:22.286
Does this mean we’re in the Union?

04:22.286 --> 04:26.628
Say what? Weren’t you listenin’
to what that brat was sayin’?

04:27.087 --> 04:30.343
We’ve gotta kill the person
with the Emblem on ‘em.

04:30.845 --> 04:31.764
Emblem?

04:34.519 --> 04:38.318
Those two goons from the other day
had gold marks on ‘em.

04:38.944 --> 04:43.119
I’m guessing that’s the Emblem
the ten members wear.

04:43.119 --> 04:46.292
And I’ve got a clue as to who’s got them.

04:46.292 --> 04:48.421
Three people off the top of my head, in fact.

04:48.421 --> 04:51.720
First is the maker
of this indestructible katana that I swiped.

04:51.720 --> 04:53.389
<i>They call ‘im “Unbreakable.”</i>

04:53.766 --> 04:59.611
<i>Second is the engineer-like guy
who experimented on me 50 years ago.</i>

04:59.611 --> 05:03.828
<i>And third was the person who nabbed me 50 years ago.</i>

05:03.828 --> 05:06.667
<i>A lady who can create invisible barriers.</i>

05:06.959 --> 05:08.629
Invisible barriers?

05:09.130 --> 05:12.679
<i>Back then, she packed my head
into her invisible barrier.</i>

05:12.679 --> 05:16.102
<i>I’m talkin’ real sturdy walls.
I was in a tight spot, literally.</i>

05:16.770 --> 05:18.858
I may be Undead,
but I’m not Unbeatable.

05:19.233 --> 05:22.574
It’s gonna be a bad matchup
if we’re up against that last lady.

05:24.744 --> 05:28.752
<i>I see... so even Zombie
has people he’s weak against.</i>

05:29.378 --> 05:31.967
<i>If we end up facing that woman, then...</i>

05:32.259 --> 05:34.388
But I don’t give a crap ‘bout any of that!

05:34.388 --> 05:38.229
No matter who gets in our way,
we’re gonna get ourselves to that lake...

05:38.396 --> 05:39.691
...and kill the mark!

05:40.358 --> 05:43.908
Nothing’s gonna keep us from our goal!

05:43.908 --> 05:47.749
Besides, we’ll be able
to make do with your unluck in a clutch.

05:47.874 --> 05:48.374
Wha-

05:48.458 --> 05:50.755
I told you that you can’t rely on my unluck!

05:50.838 --> 05:52.424
That makes it even better.

05:53.886 --> 05:58.061
Guess I’ll have to take the time to get
a feel for your rules before things get hairy.

05:58.353 --> 06:02.737
A feel? No way!
You’re gonna go all perv on me!

06:02.737 --> 06:03.446
Sure will.

06:03.488 --> 06:04.658
So honest!

06:04.950 --> 06:08.749
I’m telling you now-
do that and your likability won’t change a bit!

06:08.749 --> 06:10.962
Oh, I’m sure it will.
you’re a pushover, after all.

06:11.128 --> 06:12.381
It will not!

06:13.299 --> 06:14.218
Tee hee!

06:14.218 --> 06:16.848
Right. You just don’t change.

06:16.848 --> 06:18.393
After all, you are...

06:18.727 --> 06:21.858
...the only man in this world...
that I was able to love!

06:27.452 --> 06:28.246
- Huh?
- Huh?

06:30.500 --> 06:34.383
I know you’ll be fine,
given how you never change.

06:34.634 --> 06:36.930
You’ll make your way back to me!

06:40.896 --> 06:44.904
NO.003
HOW TO USE MY UNLUCK

06:44.904 --> 06:47.869
AUGUST 5TH

06:48.662 --> 06:52.628
<i>That was insane.
The hell attacked us?</i>

06:56.177 --> 06:59.601
<i>That’s an awful long trail of air bubbles.</i>

07:01.813 --> 07:04.359
<i>Tch... little brat’s out cold, huh?</i>

07:04.944 --> 07:11.248
<i>If she’s asphyxiating or in cardiac arrest,
each minute docks her survival rate by ten percent.</i>

07:11.583 --> 07:12.960
<i>Gotta book it!</i>

07:13.754 --> 07:17.385
<i>Her legs are caught under the wreckage, huh?
In that case...</i>

07:20.976 --> 07:24.859
<i>I’ll wedge my arm stumps in here
and grow ‘em back all at once!</i>

07:28.032 --> 07:30.746
<i>Great. Now to get topside and... mm?</i>

07:38.469 --> 07:40.975
Good. Cough up all that junk.

07:42.144 --> 07:44.816
Relax, deep breaths.

07:50.870 --> 07:54.293
Huh? Wasn’t I pinned under the boat?

07:54.459 --> 08:00.096
I’ll explain later. We’re about to get caught.
Put your hands up.

08:00.096 --> 08:00.764
Huh?

08:03.477 --> 08:05.106
A-An enemy-

08:05.106 --> 08:08.487
Undead! Do you intend to surrender?

08:08.487 --> 08:09.198
You betcha!

08:09.406 --> 08:10.993
Huh? Really?

08:10.993 --> 08:13.039
No, dummy. I’m buying time!

08:13.540 --> 08:15.001
For my little experiment.

08:16.170 --> 08:22.140
This’ll likely help us figure out...
whether your unluck can be controlled or not!

08:24.353 --> 08:25.981
Of course it can’t be controlled!

08:25.981 --> 08:27.275
That’s why I have issues in the first place!

08:27.275 --> 08:30.824
You can’t control it at will.
But I’ve got a hypothesis goin’.

08:30.824 --> 08:31.576
Huh?

08:31.910 --> 08:36.043
All your previous strokes of unluck were phenomena
that utilized things around you.

08:36.418 --> 08:40.719
<i>But what about the lightning bolt from the haircut
or the meteorite from the peck on the cheek?</i>

08:42.765 --> 08:44.393
Um, they used things from far away?

08:44.519 --> 08:45.771
Yes!

08:45.771 --> 08:48.234
You forcibly pulled in things from far away!

08:48.610 --> 08:51.031
Why did those two things happen, you ask?

08:51.031 --> 08:55.583
That’s because the haircut and the kiss
are things you have great personal value for...

08:55.583 --> 09:00.300
...and materials needed for strokes of unluck proportionate
to those values weren’t nearby!

09:01.970 --> 09:05.226
<i>Oh, God, this is so embarrassing-
it’s like he’s breaking down my views on romance.</i>

09:05.268 --> 09:06.186
So y’see...

09:06.646 --> 09:11.155
For this one, I found a source that’ll produce
a stroke of unluck proportionate to the value.

09:13.117 --> 09:17.543
And if my hunch is right,
it’s going to be one doozy of a...

09:17.752 --> 09:19.379
Huh? “For this one”?

09:21.635 --> 09:24.264
But you haven’t... wait!

09:25.643 --> 09:28.607
Huh? Why is my bra pushed up?

09:28.607 --> 09:30.026
CPR.

09:32.113 --> 09:36.998
Your pushed-up melons were in the way.
I moved them off to the side.

09:38.668 --> 09:40.463
<i>He saw them and touched them?</i>

09:40.631 --> 09:42.843
And... that’s all you did, right?

09:43.177 --> 09:47.310
Hm? Heck no.
You still weren’t coming to, so...

09:47.394 --> 09:48.270
I did it.

09:48.479 --> 09:48.980
Wha...?

09:50.692 --> 09:52.153
Mouth to mouth.

09:52.445 --> 09:54.241
N... N...

09:55.201 --> 09:59.126
No!

10:01.965 --> 10:03.384
Bingo!

10:03.384 --> 10:05.973
And now it’s time for my special move!

10:05.973 --> 10:07.727
Repair Boost!

10:09.605 --> 10:11.191
Crimson Crescent Moon!

10:14.239 --> 10:17.872
It’s a quick-draw slash that’s boosted
by my arm’s repair powers.

10:17.872 --> 10:20.501
A Japanese sword master
taught me that ages ago.

10:20.501 --> 10:22.130
I made sure not to cut up the cockpit.

10:22.422 --> 10:23.550
This puppy’s ours.

10:25.596 --> 10:27.808
Your arm... it’s...

10:27.808 --> 10:32.526
I use it as a sheath.
Quit your nitpickin’ or we’ll be here all day.

10:32.526 --> 10:33.194
Oh?

10:52.733 --> 10:53.860
How was that?

10:53.860 --> 10:55.531
Seems all we gotta do
is find a seed of unluck,

10:55.531 --> 10:58.745
and get a grasp of the contact level suitable
for triggering it. Then...

10:58.995 --> 11:04.840
Your unluck won’t be accidents,
but the best trump cards to turn things around!

11:07.721 --> 11:11.228
Now we’ve got ourselves a new means of travel.
Nice going!

11:11.228 --> 11:16.531
N-No, I’m sure this is a fluke, too!
I’m telling you, relying on me is a bad-

11:16.531 --> 11:20.288
Oh, shaddup already.
Everything went fine, so just roll with it!

11:22.835 --> 11:25.549
All right, let’s book it to Baikal!

11:25.549 --> 11:27.010
Vodka, here I come!

11:27.010 --> 11:28.888
You changed the point of the trip!

11:47.302 --> 11:50.893
<i>Self-destructing in ten, nine, eight...</i>

11:51.268 --> 11:52.354
<i>- seven, six...</i>
- Bad new!

11:53.105 --> 11:55.736
<i>...five, four, three...</i>

12:00.036 --> 12:01.915
Why’d the plane just explode like that?

12:01.915 --> 12:03.835
They figured out we swiped their ride.

12:03.835 --> 12:06.340
This isn’t the time to smile, okay?
We’re falling!

12:06.800 --> 12:10.516
No biggie! I’ve got another technique up my sleeve
from my mercenary days!

12:10.516 --> 12:11.976
We’re gonna stick a five-point landing!

12:12.143 --> 12:13.563
Five-point landing?

12:13.855 --> 12:15.400
First, the balls of your feet!

12:16.987 --> 12:18.322
Next, the sides of your calves!

12:19.826 --> 12:20.536
Then, your butt!

12:22.247 --> 12:23.249
Back!

12:24.585 --> 12:26.255
So many gross sounds!

12:26.255 --> 12:27.967
Suck it!

12:29.011 --> 12:30.179
Success.

12:30.179 --> 12:32.100
I could’ve sworn you said,
“Suck it,” at the end.

12:32.475 --> 12:33.436
No, I said, “Success.”

12:34.020 --> 12:35.816
Anyway, we landed.

12:35.816 --> 12:36.483
Huh?

12:36.483 --> 12:41.326
Be sure to watch your head.
Our mark might be around.

12:42.830 --> 12:44.499
Wow!

12:45.919 --> 12:51.681
Welcome to Lake Baikal-the world’s deepest,
clearest, and oldest freshwater lake.

12:51.681 --> 12:54.227
Apparently, folks from the organization
are gonna be here investigating a UMA.

12:54.520 --> 12:58.235
Well, I guess this is a likely spot
for a UMA to hide out, truth be told.

12:58.486 --> 13:01.366
I-It’s huge and so pretty!

13:01.366 --> 13:03.997
I guess there really is more
to the world than just Japan!

13:03.997 --> 13:04.916
Wuzzat?

13:04.916 --> 13:06.210
This your first time overseas?

13:06.210 --> 13:08.548
Uh-huh! I’ve always been a bit of a shut-in!

13:11.053 --> 13:13.474
In that case,
you should go do some sightseein’.

13:13.474 --> 13:14.184
Huh?

13:14.184 --> 13:18.527
Don’t worry. The Union won’t make
a move with all these tourists around.

13:18.527 --> 13:21.198
Operating in secret is more their style.

13:22.952 --> 13:25.498
I’m gonna go track down my old war buds.

13:25.498 --> 13:27.335
They’ll be sure to back us up when we need it.

13:27.335 --> 13:29.590
We’ll each have to fly solo for a bit.

13:30.383 --> 13:32.805
U-Um, wait a second!

13:33.723 --> 13:34.391
What’s up?

13:35.811 --> 13:38.315
About us joining the ten...

13:39.986 --> 13:42.741
Who do you think we’ll have
to take on this time?

13:42.741 --> 13:46.541
I mean... what if they’re reasonable?

13:46.583 --> 13:47.877
They’re dead meat.

13:48.127 --> 13:52.720
Courtesy of me, so I can get in.
The plan stays the same.

13:55.726 --> 13:58.732
By the way, are there any foods
you’re not keen on?

13:58.732 --> 13:59.859
Wasabi...

13:59.859 --> 14:02.322
All right, no problem, then.
It’s settled!

14:03.867 --> 14:08.334
The buddy I’m about
to bring over runs a killer restaurant!

14:10.672 --> 14:14.012
You gotta get a taste of their borscht
or else this trip’s a wash!

14:14.012 --> 14:17.101
I’ll go make some party reservations while I’m at it!

14:18.270 --> 14:20.024
You’re on your own till then, kid.

14:22.153 --> 14:24.617
You came all the way out to Russia.

14:24.617 --> 14:26.453
Don’t waste it by being your usual timid self.

14:26.788 --> 14:28.040
Have a good time!

14:32.758 --> 14:37.100
It’s only been four days since I met Zombie,
and now I’m in Russia?

14:40.106 --> 14:41.776
That’s easier said than...

14:41.943 --> 14:42.736
WHAT’S THIS?
Смотри!

14:42.820 --> 14:43.487
ARE YOU ALONE?
ты что, один?

14:43.571 --> 14:45.449
MAYBE YOU CAN HAVE TEA WITH US?
может, выпьешь с нами чаю?

14:46.536 --> 14:48.455
This is bonkers!

14:48.581 --> 14:49.917
<i>How could he be so inconsiderate?</i>

14:50.585 --> 14:54.175
<i>I can’t have fun around people with this body!</i>

14:57.265 --> 15:02.358
<i>Then again, if I hadn’t crossed paths with him,
I’d be dead by now.</i>

15:03.903 --> 15:05.322
Hmm...

15:05.322 --> 15:05.991
Huh?

15:14.466 --> 15:15.134
Oh-ho?

15:15.134 --> 15:16.386
Gah, busted!

15:17.973 --> 15:21.063
Oh, a Japanese girl? Are you a yamato nadeshiko?
Or a schoolgirl?

15:21.063 --> 15:22.356
I-I’m Japanese.

15:22.356 --> 15:24.820
Wow! The real deal!

15:26.364 --> 15:29.245
Check out my clothes!
Pretty Japanese schoolgirl-ish, right?

15:29.245 --> 15:32.836
I love Japanese schoolgirl uniforms!

15:33.128 --> 15:37.470
Um, sorry. I never went to high school,
so I wouldn’t know.

15:37.679 --> 15:41.604
Aww! But it seems like so much fun.
Such a waste!

15:41.854 --> 15:43.566
Ha, ha...

15:47.365 --> 15:50.204
Oh, wow, it’s so pretty!
Are these watercolors?

15:50.204 --> 15:53.210
Oh, how did you know?
Do you paint, too?

15:53.210 --> 15:58.930
Well, you see, I don’t get out often-if at all.
So I’ve dabbled in art here and there.

15:59.347 --> 16:01.393
Not that I’m any good at it, though.

16:03.313 --> 16:04.942
Whoa! Where’d this come from?

16:04.942 --> 16:06.571
Then let’s paint together!

16:06.571 --> 16:07.238
Huh?

16:07.698 --> 16:10.202
Um, I’m actually waiting for someone.

16:10.452 --> 16:12.248
Huh? Who is it?
Your boyfriend?

16:12.248 --> 16:15.547
That’s perfect, then! Why not surprise him
with a painting? It’d be totes emosh!

16:15.839 --> 16:16.924
Have a good time!

16:46.903 --> 16:48.531
So hey, Lil’ Lucky?

16:48.531 --> 16:49.366
Huh?

16:49.951 --> 16:54.292
Which do you like more?
Stuff that changes... or stuff that stays the same?

16:55.086 --> 16:57.758
Huh? Wait, did you just call me “Li’l Lucky”?

16:57.925 --> 16:58.885
Hee, hee!

16:58.885 --> 17:02.559
You’ve got “Good Luck” written on your cap,
so you’re Li’l Lucky!

17:05.189 --> 17:08.112
Personally, I like stuff that doesn’t change...

17:08.404 --> 17:11.744
...not tied down or swayed by anyone.

17:12.245 --> 17:14.875
Isn’t it amazing for something
to stay exactly the same?

17:18.717 --> 17:21.764
That’s why I love art.

17:22.599 --> 17:25.021
Because you can capture
the ever-changing world...

17:25.021 --> 17:27.275
...as a never-changing drawing
just like we’re doing now.

17:29.905 --> 17:32.035
So, Li’l Lucky,
which do you like?

17:32.035 --> 17:35.917
Uh... that’s a tough question.
I guess I’m...

17:39.466 --> 17:42.263
Would you mind if I thought about it for a bit?

17:42.931 --> 17:45.937
Sure! Let’s take our time and have fun!

17:57.168 --> 17:58.253
I’m done!

17:58.379 --> 18:00.424
Really? Lemme see, lemme see!

18:00.466 --> 18:02.971
Huh? U-Um...

18:02.971 --> 18:04.809
You won’t laugh, will you?

18:05.226 --> 18:07.105
I ended up adding a lot of stuff to it.

18:07.105 --> 18:09.484
Oh, that’s no big deal!
Art is all about freedom!

18:11.071 --> 18:16.081
U-Um, I wouldn’t get too close
to me if I were you.

18:18.837 --> 18:20.632
Art has no right or wrong ans-

18:25.015 --> 18:26.519
Um, so...

18:29.190 --> 18:31.737
What are those sparkles around the moon?

18:31.737 --> 18:34.367
Oh... they’re, um, well, uh...

18:35.620 --> 18:39.461
There’s nothing up in space except
for the moon and the sun, right?

18:40.045 --> 18:41.716
I learned that in school!

18:42.175 --> 18:45.014
Uh, yeah.
Nothing at all.

18:45.473 --> 18:49.899
Well, the moon looked awfully lonely up there,
so I gave it some friends.

18:51.193 --> 18:54.365
How thoughtful of you, Li’l Lucky.

18:54.825 --> 18:57.205
You’re right, the night sky
can get pretty lonely, after all.

18:57.205 --> 18:58.958
Yes, it can.

19:00.377 --> 19:04.344
Oh! By the way... about your question,
about whether I like change or not...

19:05.514 --> 19:06.599
I’ve got an answer.

19:06.849 --> 19:07.809
Ooh!

19:08.561 --> 19:14.239
For the longest time, I couldn’t change,
and it was so hard on me that I wanted to die.

19:15.074 --> 19:18.288
But four days ago,
I met this really odd guy...

19:18.413 --> 19:22.631
and it’s been crazy ever since!
He groped me all over and locked me up on the day we met!

19:22.631 --> 19:25.219
There’ve been explosions left and right,
and next thing I know, I’m here in Russia!

19:25.344 --> 19:28.560
And he never once took my ten years
as a shut-in into consideration!

19:32.568 --> 19:36.116
But... through all of that,
he helped me change.

19:38.245 --> 19:41.919
That’s why I think I was able
to draw with you today.

19:42.211 --> 19:44.090
It was so much fun.

19:44.465 --> 19:49.225
I appreciate having someone who changes me...
and changing.

19:49.810 --> 19:52.273
What lovely words.

19:53.442 --> 19:55.029
So young...

19:55.614 --> 19:56.866
So green...

19:57.576 --> 19:59.370
...and naive.

20:00.247 --> 20:01.834
Despite being all those things...

20:05.049 --> 20:09.516
Despite being all those things,
your words still resonate with me.

20:11.896 --> 20:14.400
Perhaps age has finally caught up to me.

20:29.472 --> 20:32.311
The lake... is floating?

20:36.403 --> 20:38.281
Oh, Andy!
What is that?

20:39.158 --> 20:41.287
The lake just suddenly rose up!

20:42.164 --> 20:44.127
Crimson Crescent Moon!

20:44.377 --> 20:46.841
You haven’t changed at all,
Deady Dearest.

20:48.510 --> 20:51.976
You’re going overboard with
the makeup now, Gena!

20:51.976 --> 20:53.896
Especially them crow’s feet!

20:57.696 --> 21:01.119
TA-DA
Hey, will ya look at that!
A perfect five-point landing!

21:01.119 --> 21:05.754
Now’s no time to gloat!
Can she be the most troublesome-

21:05.754 --> 21:08.926
Yup, the chick who nabbed
my ass fifty years ago.

21:10.513 --> 21:14.980
Send my beret.
I’ll play with them until the scan is done.

21:35.814 --> 21:38.068
The Boss briefed me.

21:38.736 --> 21:42.076
You want to kill me
and join the organization, right?

21:44.038 --> 21:47.086
Well then, it looks like you’ll have
to change me first.

21:47.253 --> 21:49.048
Deady Dearest...

21:50.050 --> 21:51.302
...and Li’l Lucky!

22:01.030 --> 22:06.040
TO BE CONTINUED

23:36.054 --> 23:36.805
PREVIEW

23:36.805 --> 23:40.938
<i>Is being unchanging a salvation?
Is change a sin?</i>

23:40.938 --> 23:43.569
<i>The girl’s bewilderment sinks below
the lake’s waters.</i>

23:43.819 --> 23:48.328
<i>Next episode of Undead Unluck, Episode 4-
Do You Love the Change in Me?</i> ‎

23:48.746 --> 23:50.666
<i>In search of the greatest death ever.</i>
